    "b-sks-lifecycle-intro": {
      "id": "b-sks-lifecycle-intro",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Confidence is a judgment about a specific claim, not a substitute for evidence. A claim is a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "fact",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " row: "
        },
        {
          "insert": "value",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " is the claim, "
        },
        {
          "insert": "rationale",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " is the librarian's argument for it, "
        },
        {
          "insert": "confidence",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " (0..1) says how sure we are, and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "evidence_ids",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " are the pinned observations the argument stands on. The librarian is the only writer of facts and evidence; a changed claim overwrites its live row and appends the prior version to "
        },
        {
          "insert": "fact_history",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " in the same write. This page covers how confidence is assigned and revised, the gates every fact write passes, and what happens to facts and evidence as the target underneath them drifts, is reconciled, or regresses."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-sks-lifecycle-resolution": {
      "id": "b-sks-lifecycle-resolution",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Evidence Resolution"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-sks-lifecycle-resolution-p": {
      "id": "b-sks-lifecycle-resolution-p",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "An evidence row is a pinned observation — a typed "
        },
        {
          "insert": "locator",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " into one of five stores, a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "digest",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " of the captured material, and an optional "
        },
        {
          "insert": "excerpt",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". It claims nothing itself, and citing it does not mean the material states the claim: the connection from observation to claim is the citing fact's "
        },
        {
          "insert": "rationale",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". The resolver checks every cited evidence id before the citing row is written — the locator must still resolve and the digest must still match — and reconciliation rechecks both against current inputs later."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
